#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I
"""Downloads the fonts of the trading examples (`desk` and the others that
share `crates/grid/examples/trading/`) into `crates/grid/examples/fonts/`,
one folder for all of them (gitignored: the fonts are not committed), and
the face the web pages (`crates/grid-web`) load for GPUI's default family.

    python3 -I script/fetch-example-fonts

An example's themes name families from the list below; a new family is one
more entry in `FILES`.

Every font is SIL Open Font License 1.1; each family's licence text is saved
next to its faces. Only the Regular and Bold faces are fetched, as TTF, and
of IBM Plex Sans only Regular: GPUI's web platform draws its default family,
`.SystemUIFont`, in IBM Plex Sans, and the web pages load it for the text no
theme styles (a drag's view, which GPUI draws outside the window's root,
such as gpui-kit's dock tab); without it, laying that text out panics. Each
URL is pinned to a commit or a release tag, and every file is checked against
its SHA-256 below before it is written. A file already present with the right
hash is not downloaded again.

Two families come from a release archive (Inter, Iosevka). Only the archive's
directory and the two faces are read, with HTTP range requests, not the whole
archive (Iosevka's is 120 MB); a server without range requests gets the whole
archive downloaded once instead.

Without these fonts the examples run with the system's monospace font and
say so once on stderr.
"""

import hashlib
import http.client
import io
import pathlib
import sys
import urllib.request
import zipfile

ROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
DEST = ROOT / "crates" / "grid" / "examples" / "fonts"

